    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d278">

                <pb facs="0380" n="370" xml:id="pg370"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">800.796/527: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in the United Kingdom</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Winant</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                        State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">London</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1944-02-04T01:00:00+01:00">February 4, 1944—1
                            a.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received February 3—9:38 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>968. Embassy learns from reliable source that this morning Foreign Office
                    received a telegram from the British Embassy in Washington reporting that the
                    United States Government was now ready to begin discussions looking toward the
                    conclusion of a general civil air agreement. The message stated that the Embassy
                    had been requested in an <hi rendition="#italic">aide-mémoire</hi> from the
                    Department to suggest an agenda. This subject was discussed this afternoon in a
                    meeting in Lord Beaver-brook’s office, attended by his staff, Air Ministry,
                    Foreign Office and service officials. It is understood that these officials
                    believe they will be ready to begin discussions in 6 to 8 weeks (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">id est</hi>, prepare and secure approval of the
                    agenda).</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Winant</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
